{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/445125-healing-wounds-no-not-those-wounds-shadow-wounds","id":445125,"title":"Healing Wounds (no, not those wounds... Shadow Wounds)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-16T18:07:18-07:00","id":445125,"title":"Healing Wounds (no, not those wounds... Shadow Wounds)","content":"Hi,<br /> <br /> This may be a really simple thing to answer, though I can't seem to find any information on it... Can the Uratha heal up a Wound? These places are really really bad and having not yet grabbed Werewolf v2 yet I'm not sure what is mentioned about these dark infected places of the Shadow... But I was wondering if doing such a thing was possible, or perhaps quarantining the area and how easy would it be? I'm thinking on character Aspirations and I believe repairing a Wound would be a great long-term one to take potentially, but how would a Pack go about it? Is it even possible to right such a thing when it has occured?<br /> <br /> I mainly want to give a reason for a character to enter one (because they have awesome game effects I'd like the character to fight through) and also have some kind of long-term goal for them. So, I was wondering how people here would go about involving a Wound into character's goals and arcs and how they could fit around something long-term, being as they're such an inherently tainted piece of the Shadow.<br /> <br /> Thanks for any replies. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-16T18:26:35-07:00","id":445150,"title":"","content":"Yes, they can be healed. In fact there's at least one Lodge based around the concept and even a Hunter compact that try to do it.<br /> <br /> As for how, it seems like you'd want to repair the area on both sides. This may involve putting things to rest as best as possible, burying all the bodies and letting all the dirty secrets out, and attempting to make its physical representation a better place. On the Shadow side you'll have to deal with binding or destroying Wound spirits, especially the Lord that is supposed to be at the center of wounds. You'll probably want to sacrifice or alter loci within the wound, so they stop spewing out Essence tainted with malevolence. The specifics are going to depend on the individual Wound and it should take a long time but it's doable.<br /> <br /> There may be rules for it in one of the books., but if there are I don't know them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 03-16-2015, 09:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}